1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,625
Hi — I'm Divij Pawar. This is part two of When Two

2
00:00:02,625 --> 00:00:03,458
Agents Disagree.

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:07,792
Last time: correctness needs ground truth, disagreement needs nothing, and the safe

4
00:00:07,792 --> 00:00:10,375
move is to surface a conflict rather than resolve it.

5
00:00:11,083 --> 00:00:13,500
This time I'll show you what I actually built on top of

6
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,833
that — three files, twenty-one tests, and nothing else in the system

7
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:17,633
changed.

8
00:00:18,010 --> 00:00:20,718
Here's the whole thing in one breath. I already had an accountability

9
00:00:20,718 --> 00:00:23,802
layer that made an agent's reasoning permanently on the record — but

10
00:00:23,802 --> 00:00:26,052
it could only prove what was said, never whether it was true.

11
00:00:26,677 --> 00:00:30,635
Cross-agent validation was already on the architecture diagram: specified, named,

12
00:00:30,635 --> 00:00:34,093
and completely empty. So I built the smallest honest version. Run two

13
00:00:34,093 --> 00:00:37,510
agents, compare their numbers, write down where they disagree, and stop. No

14
00:00:37,510 --> 00:00:39,343
judge. No model. Set arithmetic.

15
00:00:40,110 --> 00:00:41,402
Four things already existed.

16
00:00:41,777 --> 00:00:45,485
The ReasoningObject — one frozen record per agent attempt, holding the conclusion,

17
00:00:45,652 --> 00:00:47,277
the steps, the confidence, the sources.

18
00:00:47,985 --> 00:00:51,235
The validation loop — output must parse into a required structure, one

19
00:00:51,235 --> 00:00:54,402
retry, then halt; both attempts get recorded either way, because a failed

20
00:00:54,402 --> 00:00:55,568
attempt is evidence too.

21
00:00:56,152 --> 00:00:57,443
The store — SQLite, with

22
00:00:57,818 --> 00:01:01,277
database-level triggers that abort any update or delete, so you cannot quietly

23
00:01:01,277 --> 00:01:02,110
edit history.

24
00:01:02,693 --> 00:01:06,318
And the consistency probe, which already had the scoring: sixty percent number

25
00:01:06,318 --> 00:01:10,568
overlap, forty percent word overlap, three thresholds. All of that existed.

26
00:01:10,943 --> 00:01:13,693
It was just pointed at one agent, compared against a repeat of

27
00:01:13,693 --> 00:01:14,493
itself.

28
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:17,298
So I audited the project to find where this could actually be

29
00:01:17,298 --> 00:01:20,673
useful, and the answer was already on the published architecture diagram.

30
00:01:21,423 --> 00:01:23,507
The orchestration layer declared three mechanisms:

31
00:01:23,965 --> 00:01:24,840
cross-agent validation,

32
00:01:25,215 --> 00:01:27,340
dynamic task allocation, pattern recognition.

33
00:01:27,757 --> 00:01:29,173
All three had zero implementation.

34
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:31,423
But cross-agent validation was the

35
00:01:31,798 --> 00:01:34,840
best-specified orphan in the repo — twenty-one thousand, eight hundred and

36
00:01:34,882 --> 00:01:39,507
twenty-four bytes of specification, sixteen scaffolded scripts, and zero shared

37
00:01:39,507 --> 00:01:41,882
logic connecting them. That's the pattern everywhere.

38
00:01:42,382 --> 00:01:45,840
The node layer is thirty thousand, four hundred and ninety-seven lines; one

39
00:01:45,882 --> 00:01:49,590
thousand two hundred and seventy-six of those are real logic. Tests: zero.

40
00:01:49,923 --> 00:01:51,173
And why had nobody built it?

41
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:54,965
Cross-agent validation needs two agents that emit comparable conclusions.

42
00:01:55,382 --> 00:01:57,215
The project had approximately zero.

43
00:01:57,930 --> 00:02:00,597
Version one got scoped down until it was almost boring, and the

44
00:02:00,597 --> 00:02:01,430
cuts are the design.

45
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:05,763
Producer A: a real agent, already wired to live SEC EDGAR endpoints.

46
00:02:05,805 --> 00:02:08,972
Producer B: a hand-written fixture that returns a conclusion I pick in

47
00:02:08,972 --> 00:02:10,472
advance. That sounds like cheating.

48
00:02:10,888 --> 00:02:14,138
It isn't. If both producers are real and the comparator says contradiction,

49
00:02:14,430 --> 00:02:17,722
you can't tell whether they genuinely disagree or your comparator is broken.

50
00:02:18,097 --> 00:02:18,897
With a fixture,

51
00:02:19,305 --> 00:02:21,513
a wrong result can only be the comparator's fault.

52
00:02:22,055 --> 00:02:26,513
Second cut: contradiction means numeric divergence only. No entailment model, no

53
00:02:26,513 --> 00:02:27,313
judge.

54
00:02:27,222 --> 00:02:30,013
Third cut: it writes a record and stops — no escalation, no

55
00:02:30,013 --> 00:02:33,888
alert. And no new HTTP route: the layer has four open critical

56
00:02:33,888 --> 00:02:37,180
security findings, and adding no route adds no new exposure.

57
00:02:37,890 --> 00:02:40,223
Three files, and the test file is the biggest of them —

58
00:02:40,223 --> 00:02:41,473
that ratio isn't an accident.

59
00:02:41,973 --> 00:02:45,723
Each agent gets its own context: information asymmetry, encoded in a function

60
00:02:45,723 --> 00:02:46,523
signature.

61
00:02:46,807 --> 00:02:50,015
When an agent fails validation twice, the loop raises, and its records

62
00:02:50,015 --> 00:02:52,765
get carried forward rather than dropped, because a halt is a fact

63
00:02:52,765 --> 00:02:53,973
somebody may want to see.

64
00:02:54,473 --> 00:02:58,223
Then the comparison, in full: extract the numbers from both conclusions, take

65
00:02:58,223 --> 00:02:59,182
the symmetric difference,

66
00:02:59,848 --> 00:03:01,973
and anything in exactly one of them is a divergence.

67
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:04,348
No model. No judge. Set arithmetic.

68
00:03:04,848 --> 00:03:08,765
The scoring wasn't rewritten, it was re-pointed — same weights, same thresholds,

69
00:03:08,765 --> 00:03:13,098
imported unmodified. And one line covers both cases: a different value is

70
00:03:13,098 --> 00:03:15,473
caught, and a missing number is caught by the same rule.

71
00:03:16,250 --> 00:03:18,792
Now, how it lives inside the layer rather than beside it.

72
00:03:19,208 --> 00:03:22,250
Both agents share one run ID, because here the comparison is the

73
00:03:22,250 --> 00:03:25,833
evidence — flag a contradiction without producing both conclusions and you've

74
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:27,792
published an accusation with no exhibits.

75
00:03:28,458 --> 00:03:31,542
The runs table stores a free-form JSON blob, so a whole new

76
00:03:31,542 --> 00:03:34,000
kind of record needed no migration and no new column.

77
00:03:34,375 --> 00:03:37,958
One new key. And it inherits the append-only triggers for free: once

78
00:03:37,958 --> 00:03:38,792
a flag is written,

79
00:03:39,375 --> 00:03:42,750
it can't be updated or deleted. Then, the tests. Twenty-one new, all

80
00:03:42,750 --> 00:03:46,000
passing — which is worth almost nothing. A passing suite proves your

81
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:48,458
tests agree with your code, not that they'd notice if the code

82
00:03:48,458 --> 00:03:50,000
were wrong. So I broke it on purpose.

83
00:03:50,625 --> 00:03:53,625
Swap the symmetric difference for an intersection: seven tests fail.

84
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:57,292
Return false instead of null when no comparison happened: three more.

85
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,770
So let's be precise about what this is not.

86
00:04:00,145 --> 00:04:04,145
Comparison is numeric only — two conclusions that disagree completely while citing

87
00:04:04,145 --> 00:04:06,020
the same figures sail straight through.

88
00:04:06,478 --> 00:04:09,812
Producer B is still a fixture, so no genuine disagreement has ever

89
00:04:09,812 --> 00:04:11,145
been observed on live data.

90
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:12,320
It

91
00:04:11,978 --> 00:04:14,978
isn't SQL-queryable. And a flagged contradiction triggers nothing.

92
00:04:15,620 --> 00:04:18,703
Your turn. Paste this into Claude: "Find one place in my system

93
00:04:18,703 --> 00:04:21,370
where a check returns false when it actually means the check could

94
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:22,170
not run."

95
00:04:22,328 --> 00:04:23,128
That's the

96
00:04:22,995 --> 00:04:26,245
null-versus-false distinction, aimed at your own code. False claims a check happened

97
00:04:26,245 --> 00:04:27,120
and came back clean.

98
00:04:27,662 --> 00:04:28,828
Null says the check couldn't run.

99
00:04:29,245 --> 00:04:31,787
A system that silently converts the second into the first

100
00:04:32,162 --> 00:04:34,787
manufactures an all-clear out of a failure. Go find one.

101
00:04:35,628 --> 00:04:39,670
Three files. Twenty-one tests. Nothing else changed. The judgment stays with the

102
00:04:39,670 --> 00:04:42,503
human — that was never the bottleneck. That was the point. Divij

103
00:04:42,503 --> 00:04:43,303
Pawar.
